The  command  is used to examine and debug system images.  If run
without any arguments, operates on the running system.   The  op‐
tions are as follows: Operate on the specified crash dump instead
of the default Crash dumps should be from the same version of the
system  and  same  machine architecture as the running version of
and must be uncompressed.  Extract the name list from the  speci‐
fied  kernel  instead of the default Enable writing.  The command
syntax used by is the same as the in‐kernel  debugger.   See  the
manual page for more information.  Operations and facilities that
require  a running system, such as breakpoints, are not supported
by does not provide pagination.  However, by using the pipe  sym‐
bol,  output  may  be  sent to commands available from the shell.
For example: crash> ps | more crash> ps | grep  ioflush  You  can
obtain  a  full  list  of  all  kernel  stack traces with a shell
pipeline like the following: # echo ps | crash | grep ’ˆ[0‐9]’  |
cut ‐c 30‐46 | \
  sed  ’s,ˆ,bt/a  ,’  | crash The command appeared in The command
